    "description": "ALLETE is a utility holding company whose businesses include Minnesota Power, Superior Water, Light and Power, ALLETE Clean Energy, BNI Energy, and New Energy Equity. Its customer base spans regulated electric and water customers, municipal and cooperative utilities, and renewable-energy counterparties. The company combines regulated utility earnings with asset-heavy owned generation, fuel, and clean-energy development businesses, giving it a mix of contracted and regulated cash flows. Its principal operating footprint is in Minnesota, Wisconsin, and North Dakota, with clean-energy activities extending beyond those core utility jurisdictions. ALLETE reported 1,616 employees at year-end 2024 and described a diversified platform of utility, renewable, and energy-services businesses. The company was taken private in December 2025 by CPP Investments and Global Infrastructure Partners following the merger agreement announced in May 2024.",
